<div class="legal-body">
  <p class="intro">This privacy policy describes how Creapolis collects, uses, stores and protects your personal data when you interact with Creapolis — whether through our website (creapolis.dev), or any of our mobile applications (Solennix, Pikle, Películas and future apps). If anything is unclear, write to us at <a href="mailto:hola@creapolis.dev">hola@creapolis.dev</a>.</p>

  <p class="lang-note">También disponible en <a href="/privacidad">español</a>.</p>

  <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
  <p>
    The data controller for the personal data collected through our products is Creapolis, a software development studio operated by
    <strong>Tiago David Furtado</strong>, based in Monterrey, Nuevo León, Mexico.
    Contact: <a href="mailto:hola@creapolis.dev">hola@creapolis.dev</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Scope</h2>
  <p>This policy applies to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Website creapolis.dev:</strong> browsing, contact form and editorial content.</li>
    <li><strong>Mobile applications:</strong> Solennix, Pikle (Pepinillo), Películas, and any future application published by Creapolis on Google Play Store or Apple App Store.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>When a section applies only to the website or only to the apps, we indicate it explicitly. If not indicated, it applies to both.</p>

  <h2>3. What data we collect</h2>

  <h3>3.1 Website</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact data:</strong> name, email, company (optional) — only if you write to us via the form or direct email.</li>
    <li><strong>Message content:</strong> whatever you include when describing your project or inquiry.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical browsing data:</strong> IP address, device type, browser, pages visited — used exclusively for aggregated performance metrics.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.2 Mobile apps — Account data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>When you register:</strong> name, email, encrypted password, phone (optional).</li>
    <li><strong>Third-party authentication:</strong> if you use Google Sign-In or Apple Sign-In, we only receive your name and verified email.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.3 Mobile apps — Operational data</h3>
  <p>Depending on the app you use, we may process data you voluntarily enter:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Event &amp; task management:</strong> titles, descriptions, dates, times, locations, notes, statuses, checklists.</li>
    <li><strong>CRM / contacts:</strong> names, phones, emails, addresses and notes of your clients.</li>
    <li><strong>Quotes &amp; contracts:</strong> concepts, prices, terms, statuses.</li>
    <li><strong>Inventory:</strong> items, quantities, statuses, usage history.</li>
    <li><strong>Statistics &amp; metrics:</strong> data the app calculates from your information (revenue, averages, activity).</li>
    <li><strong>Photos &amp; files:</strong> images or documents you attach within the app.</li>
    <li><strong>Preferences:</strong> app settings, themes, notifications.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.4 Technical &amp; usage data (apps)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Device information:</strong> model, OS and version, language, timezone.</li>
    <li><strong>Crash reports:</strong> error logs and unexpected closures sent to Firebase Crashlytics. These do not contain personally identifiable information.</li>
    <li><strong>Anonymized analytics:</strong> screens visited, usage frequency, features used. Aggregated data that does not identify individual users.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.5 Data we do NOT collect</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not access your phone contacts, messages, call history or gallery without your explicit consent.</li>
    <li>We do not collect real-time location.</li>
    <li>We do not collect sensitive data: racial origin, health, religious beliefs, sexual orientation, biometric information.</li>
    <li>We do not sell, rent or share your personal data for advertising purposes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. How we use your data</h2>
  <p>We use your data exclusively to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Provide the service:</strong> make the app work according to its purpose (event management, productivity, entertainment, etc.).</li>
    <li><strong>Sync across devices:</strong> keep your data updated if you use the app on multiple devices.</li>
    <li><strong>Respond to inquiries (website):</strong> prepare proposals, follow up on projects.</li>
    <li><strong>Improve the service:</strong> analyze errors (Crashlytics) and anonymized usage patterns.</li>
    <li><strong>Communication:</strong> notifications about your account, subscription or service changes. We do not send marketing without your consent.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal compliance:</strong> respond to valid requests from competent authorities.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>Our apps and website use the following services that may process technical data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Firebase (Google):</strong> Crashlytics (crash reports) and Analytics (anonymized analytics). <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Play Billing / Apple App Store (StoreKit):</strong> payment and subscription processing. We do not have access to your full credit card data; the transaction is processed by the platform.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Sign-In / Apple Sign-In:</strong> optional authentication. We only receive your name and verified email.</li>
    <li><strong>Infrastructure providers:</strong> hosting, cloud storage and email services, under confidentiality agreements.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These services may operate outside of Mexico. By using our apps, you accept international data transfers under these providers' conditions.</p>

  <h2>6. How we store and protect your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>On your device:</strong> data is stored securely using native OS encryption (Keychain on iOS, EncryptedSharedPreferences on Android).</li>
    <li><strong>In the cloud:</strong> if you use sync, data is transmitted and stored encrypted (TLS 1.2+ / HTTPS) on servers compliant with recognized standards (SOC 2, ISO 27001).</li>
    <li><strong>Passwords:</strong> stored encrypted using secure hashing (bcrypt / Argon2). Never in plain text.</li>
    <li><strong>Restricted access:</strong> only authorized Creapolis personnel access data, under confidentiality agreements.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>No system is infallible. If a security incident affecting your data were to occur, we would notify you as soon as possible along with the measures taken.</p>

  <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account and operational data:</strong> retained while your account is active. Deleted within 30 days of your account deletion request.</li>
    <li><strong>Crash and analytics data:</strong> retained for a maximum of 90 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Billing data:</strong> retained by the payment platform (Google Play / App Store) per their own policies.</li>
    <li><strong>Website inquiries:</strong> contact data and messages retained up to 2 years from last interaction, or until you request deletion.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Account and data deletion</h2>
  <p>
    If you created an account in any of our apps, you can delete it at any time along with all associated data:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>From the app:</strong> Settings → Account → Delete account.</li>
    <li><strong>From the web:</strong> <a href="/eliminar-cuenta">creapolis.dev/eliminar-cuenta</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>By email:</strong> <a href="mailto:hola@creapolis.dev">hola@creapolis.dev</a> with subject "Delete my account" from the associated email address.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Deletion is irreversible. All your operational data is removed within 30 days. Anonymous aggregated data may be retained. See full details on the <a href="/eliminar-cuenta">account deletion page</a>.</p>

  <h2>9. Sharing data with third parties</h2>
  <p>We do not sell, rent or share personal data for commercial purposes. We only share data when:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Service providers:</strong> process data on our behalf under confidentiality agreements (see section 5).</li>
    <li><strong>Legal requirement:</strong> court order, competent authority request, or protection of our legal rights.</li>
    <li><strong>With your consent:</strong> when you give us explicit permission.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>10. Your rights</h2>
  <p>In accordance with applicable legislation, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you.</li>
    <li><strong>Rectify</strong> inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
    <li><strong>Cancel</strong> the processing of your data.</li>
    <li><strong>Object</strong> to the use of your data for specific purposes.</li>
    <li><strong>Portability:</strong> request your data in a structured, commonly used format.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete your account</strong> and all associated data.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise these rights: <a href="mailto:hola@creapolis.dev">hola@creapolis.dev</a> with subject "Exercise of ARCO rights". We respond within 20 business days as required by Mexican law (LFPDPPP).
  </p>
  <p>
    Users in the European Union may exercise rights under GDPR. Users in California, under CCPA. The contact point is the same.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our apps are not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from children. If you are a parent or guardian and detect that a minor has provided us with data, contact us at <a href="mailto:hola@creapolis.dev">hola@creapolis.dev</a> and we will delete it immediately.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Push notifications</h2>
  <p>
    Our apps may send push notifications for reminders, event alerts or subscription updates. You can disable them at any time from your device settings.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Third-party links</h2>
  <p>Our apps and website contain links to external platforms (app stores, social networks, tools). We are not responsible for those services' privacy policies.</p>

  <h2>14. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy periodically. We will notify you about significant changes through the app or via email. The current version is always available on this page with its update date. Continued use after a modification implies acceptance.</p>

  <h2>15. Applicable law</h2>
  <p>
    This policy is governed by the Federal Law on Protection of Personal Data Held by Private Parties (LFPDPPP) of Mexico. We also comply with GDPR (EU) and CCPA (California) as applicable. Disputes: competent courts of Monterrey, Nuevo León.
  </p>

  <h2>16. Contact</h2>
  <p>For any questions, complaints or exercise of rights regarding your personal data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:hola@creapolis.dev">hola@creapolis.dev</a></li>
    <li><strong>Responsible:</strong> Tiago David Furtado — Creapolis</li>
    <li><strong>Address:</strong> Monterrey, Nuevo León, Mexico</li>
    <li><strong>Delete account:</strong> <a href="/eliminar-cuenta">creapolis.dev/eliminar-cuenta</a></li>
  </ul>
</div>

